# Known-broken links caused by upstream @takazudo/zudo-doc limitations, not by
# this project's content. Every entry must name the upstream issue and be
# removable once that issue ships a fix.
#
# Entry forms:
#   file:line:href   pins one occurrence (precise, but breaks if lines shift)
#   href=<href>      allows that href wherever it appears
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# zudolab/zudo-doc#3196 — the version switcher offers a snapshot link for a
# page that exists only in newer docs instead of greying it out. The
# VersionSwitcher component supports `unavailableVersions`, but
# `buildInlineVersionSwitcher` never computes it.
#
# Concretely: the changelog entries below exist in Latest and in the 2.0
# snapshot but not in 1.0 (which predates them), so every page rendering a
# version switcher for them emits a dead /v/1.0/ link — 32 links across the EN
# and JA trees, from both the header switcher (line ~109) and the in-content
# one (line ~1003).
#
# Not redirectable, unlike the other two cases now handled in public/_redirects
# (the versions-page entry slug, and the unversioned /docs/claude* tree): there
# is no correct destination here, because the page genuinely does not exist in
# 1.0. Silently landing the reader on a different changelog entry would be
# worse than the 404.
#
# The href= form is deliberate — pinning 32 line numbers across changelog pages
# would rot on the next changelog edit, silently turning this into a no-op.
href=/v/1.0/docs/changelog/v1.1.0-next.1
href=/v/1.0/docs/changelog/v1.1.0-next.2
href=/v/1.0/docs/changelog/v1.1.0-next.3
href=/v/1.0/docs/changelog/v2.0.0
href=/v/1.0/ja/docs/changelog/v1.1.0-next.1
href=/v/1.0/ja/docs/changelog/v1.1.0-next.2
href=/v/1.0/ja/docs/changelog/v1.1.0-next.3
href=/v/1.0/ja/docs/changelog/v2.0.0

